Apple's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/28/apple-new-macbook-pro/">new 14-inch and 16-inch MacBook Pro</a> models feature an upgraded six-speaker sound system, with redesigned woofers and tweeters, along with dedicated audio tuning for use with the lid closed.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/Apple-MacBook-Pro-with-PROLED-XDR-Display-audio-system-scaled.jpg" alt="" width="2560" height="1440" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1074070" /><br/>
<br/>
Apple says the new woofer design delivers 50% deeper bass, while redesigned tweeters improve clarity by shaping how sound disperses. The system continues to support Spatial Audio with Dolby Atmos.<br/>
<br/>
For the first time, Apple has also added dedicated audio tuning for closed-lid use. The company says this improves sound quality when the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-pro/">MacBook Pro</a> is connected to an external display, allowing users to continue using its built-in speakers in a desktop setup.<br/>
<br/>
